Architecture lock completed — 20 September 2026

Main now contains a binding approved architecture amendment:
docs/architecture/CEAC_OS_Architecture_Approved_Amendment_2026-09-20.md

Main commit: 71b295d53a782d44e45834eb00f54442ca6775e5

AGENTS.md now requires every coding agent to read that amendment before touching work types, templates, people/profile, reports, Manager Home, Team, or Admin People.

Locked decisions include:
- no generative AI / LLM dependency anywhere in CEAC OS;
- deterministic intelligence through context, rules, templates, recurrence, prefill, calculations and exception detection;
- one shared Work Engine with seven behaviour-specific types: Task, Routine, Case, Request, Decision, Meeting outcome, Deliverable;
- Routine means recurrence now;
- first-class template library + deterministic repeated-work template suggestions, always human-confirmed;
- template edits never rewrite historical work;
- Manager copy/work-type explanations/Add another step/My Work wording/Manager's summary;
- Team and Admin People grouping by actual sub-team membership without turning sub-teams into rigid silos;
- full employee/HR record model for every role;
- Ghana Card front/back + details, SSNIT, tax, next-of-kin, certificates and bank/payment data under HR verification;
- verified sensitive data cannot be directly overwritten by the employee;
- protected storage and no permanent public links for sensitive documents;
- Admin & HR full authorised employee record; managers do not automatically see sensitive identity/payroll data;
- typed-work, templates and HR record backend contracts added to Claude's future migration roadmap.

The amendment also records the live-schema relationship so nobody should fake unsupported client features.

PR #4 has been reconciled with the new main architecture and is 0 commits behind main. It remains open and unmerged.
